      "description": "Occupant load is one of the most important life safety factors in a building, and it affects far more than the width of exits.\n\nIn this video, we explore how the occupant load impacts:\n• Occupancy classification\n• Construction type requirements\n• Automatic sprinkler systems\n• Fire alarm systems\n• Number of required exits\n• Exit and egress sizing\n• Door swing direction\n• Panic and fire exit hardware\n\nUsing new assembly occupancies as examples, this overview explains why occupant load must be calculated accurately and maintained.\n\nFor more guidance, check out this blog: https://www.nfpa.org/news-blogs-and-articles/blogs/2020/04/06/how-to-calculate-occupant-load \n\nImportant Notice:\nAny opinion expressed in this video is the opinion of the author and does not necessarily represent the official position of NFPA or its Technical Committees. In addition, this piece is neither intended nor should it be relied upon to provide professional consultation or services.",
